From: RainWrt maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] nvmem: qfprom: keep IPQ5018 MMIO byte reads

Forward-port the hardware-verified kmiit fix by ByteArray0,
4299001bcfebba0d5d295818937a92b436f3f9ed. 32-bit MMIO reads on this
SoC caused reboot loops. Keep upstream cell alignment and other SoCs'
access width; use byte accesses only on IPQ5018. No thermal trip bypass.

--- a/drivers/nvmem/qfprom.c
+++ b/drivers/nvmem/qfprom.c
@@ -329,6 +329,14 @@ static int qfprom_reg_read(void *context,
 	if (read_raw_data && priv->qfpraw)
 		base = priv->qfpraw;
 
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(priv->dev->of_node, "qcom,ipq5018-qfprom")) {
+		u8 *byte_val = _val;
+
+		for (i = 0; i < bytes; i++)
+			byte_val[i] = readb(base + reg + i);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	for (i = 0; i < words; i++)
 		*val++ = readl(base + reg + i * sizeof(u32));
 
